  "notes": "USAGE:\nOriginally a military term, {撤退|てったい} is now widely used in business for exiting a market, closing operations, or pulling out of a venture. It implies an organized, deliberate withdrawal rather than a chaotic retreat.\n\nCOMPARISON WITH SIMILAR WORDS:\n- {撤退|てったい}: organized withdrawal (military or business)\n- {退却|たいきゃく}: retreat (more military, sometimes implies defeat)\n- {撤収|てっしゅう}: removal, cleanup; pulling out equipment/personnel\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {市場|しじょう}から{撤退|てったい}する: to withdraw from a market\n- {撤退|てったい}を{決|き}める: to decide to withdraw\n- {全面|ぜんめん}{撤退|てったい}: full withdrawal\n- {撤退|てったい}{戦略|せんりゃく}: withdrawal strategy",
